@startuml goal-loop
!theme plain
title Goal loop: caller/board authorship (D-GOALS); agent self-goals deferred to SH2+ G2
' Updated: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13)

actor "Initiating caller" as Caller
participant "Launcher" as L
participant "Optional board/orchestrator" as B
participant "Session host\n(goal ledger, admission)" as SH
participant "Goal provider\n(scheduler)" as GP
participant "Current registered runner\n(agent account)" as R
participant "Harness\n(agent)" as H

note over Caller, H
  Authority and ordering only: goal-client actions/capability shape,
  runner proof and goal-free completion path remain unpublished.
  Session host §3.8 owns the joint publication/qualification gates.
  Goal absence never blocks launch, attach, delivery, wake, stop or recovery.
  SH1 retains its existing optional board compatibility seam.
end note
alt initial goal supplied by launching caller
  Caller -> L: initial goal with admitted start
  L -> SH: caller-authored initial goal; authenticated attribution
else optional board goal revision
  B -> SH: board-owned revision (CAS, slot)
end
SH -> SH: host admission; caller authority, current revision, bounded budget;\nagent executor gains no goal-authoring capability
SH -> SH: persist revision durably
SH -> R: at turn boundary, deliver to current-epoch registered runner
R -> H: admitted goal input
H --> R: harness acknowledgement
R --> SH: acknowledgement
SH --> Caller: applied, deferred or rolled back with joined error

loop while authorised goal active and budget available
  H -> R: turn completed; idle
  R -> SH: current execution state
  GP -> SH: schedule nudge for committed revision
  SH -> SH: revision, budget and interval checks; host admission
  SH -> R: host-authored nudge frame; goal text keeps author's provenance
  R -> H: continue toward caller/board goal
end
note over GP, H
  Pending interactions suspend nudges and turn counting.
  No-progress detector remains shadow-only until its activation gate.
  CAS, budgets and outcome ownership are retained (GOL §§3–5).
end note
opt board bound, agent reports outcome
  H -> B: outcome proposal or blocked notice through retained board seam
  B -> B: board owner accepts/refuses; only it changes goal revision/state
end
opt passive park note
  H -> SH: park note through existing tail/bridge path
  SH -> SH: local agent-authored note; no goal revision
end
note over R, H
  Session-token possession gives no goal capability.
  Self-goal set/clear/status and board-free agent completion are not enabled.
  G2 later chooses bounded self-goals or caller/board authorship only.
end note
@enduml
